Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 18:44:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 047/154] refactor: the last native accessors leave the window
 body
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HasRealizedWindow and SetExcludedFromWindowCycling have portable signatures
and platform-shaped bodies, so they go on the seam. Their CHECKs are copied
across unchanged - they state that an Atrium window is always in-process, and
that is not something to soften for tidiness.

GetNSWindowForAnimation cannot go on the seam: its signature names an AppKit
type. It moves to atrium_browser_window_mac.mm instead, with a comment saying
why it stays whole. Its only caller asks about a parent it has every reason to
expect realised.

Verified by little-window-hotkey 2 of 2 and devtools-dock 2 of 2 - Cmd+Q and
window creation, which is the Hide and cycling path these two serve.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index 35583f7ee0e58..22c272de81112 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -3508,6 +3508,7 @@ static_library("ui") {
       "atrium/atrium_window_platform_mac.mm",
       "atrium/atrium_native_widget_mac.h",
       "atrium/atrium_native_widget_mac.mm",
+      "atrium/atrium_browser_window_mac.mm",
       "atrium/atrium_window_metrics.h",
       "atrium/atrium_browser_window.h",
       "atrium/atrium_browser_window.mm",
